
<Defs xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="rimworld DefsSchema.xsd" xmlns="rimworld">

	<!--
		Arrogant (2026-09-23). A plain personality trait, forced by the reptile dragons'
		pride gene (Reptiles, PMM_GeneTrait_DragonPride), and free for any of the family's
		mods to force later.

		commonality 0 is what keeps it off random pawns. A TraitDef that never states a
		commonality is already 0 and never gets handed out by the pawn generator (the
		reason mod traits "never appear" when the field is forgotten), so writing 0 says
		that on purpose: only a gene can give this one out.

		socialFightChanceFactor is the field Bloodlust uses for the same kind of friction
		in an argument. The rest of its behaviour cannot live in XML, because a TraitDef
		cannot read another pawn's state: how much she looks down on a pawn is decided in
		Source/ProjectMamono/ArrogantTraitPatch.cs, where her opinion of anyone below her
		ISEKAI level is docked and her chance to pick an insult over small talk rises.
		That file holds the two numbers, so tuning them is one edit each.

		The same file also puts the penalty on screen. Vanilla builds the Social tab's
		opinion breakdown by listing the contributions it knows about, so a patched total
		moved the number with no reason beside it; a second patch appends the missing line
		(" - Arrogant (they are 6 levels lower): -6") in the engine's own shape, and only
		while the penalty applies. Its wording is a keyed translation
		(Languages/English/Keyed/ArrogantTrait.xml), and the trait label inside it comes from
		this def, so renaming the trait renames the line. It reads the degree's label rather
		than the def's own, because a def with degrees and no label of its own has an empty
		LabelCap - and an empty one is invisible rather than obvious.

		No market value offset: it used vanilla's "people dislike her" idiom (Abrasive,
		AnnoyingVoice) until 2026-09-23, when the level-based opinion took its place.
		It is mutually exclusive with vanilla's Kind, declared below and, for the pawn
		generator's side of it, in Patches/Trait_ArrogantConflicts.xml.
	-->
	<TraitDef>
		<defName>PMM_Arrogant</defName>
		<!-- Both kinds of label are needed. This one is the trait's own name; each degree below
		     carries the name a player actually reads. A TraitDef that has degrees and no label
		     of its own has an empty Def.LabelCap, which is why the opinion line in
		     ArrogantOpinionExplanationPatch first went out naming no trait at all (2026-09-23). -->
		<label>arrogant</label>
		<commonality>0</commonality>
		<degreeDatas>
			<li>
				<label>arrogant</label>
				<description>{PAWN_nameDef} is sure {PAWN_pronoun} is better than everyone else, and looks down on anyone of a lower level. {PAWN_pronoun} thinks less of them, and is quicker to insult them than to be civil.</description>
				<socialFightChanceFactor>1.5</socialFightChanceFactor>
			</li>
		</degreeDatas>
		<!-- Kind and arrogant are opposites (2026-09-23, user ruling). Vanilla's Kind
		     lists Abrasive and Psychopath; this half of the pair is declared here and the
		     other half in Patches/Trait_ArrogantConflicts.xml, the way vanilla's Greedy
		     and Jealous name each other. -->
		<conflictingTraits>
			<li>Kind</li>
		</conflictingTraits>
	</TraitDef>

</Defs>
